     from Apache FOP 2.11: a test of hook page-master-by-content (fop/CR-017). -->
<testcase>
  <info>
    <p>
      A marked FO that produces no line still starts its part at the next content: an empty fo:block (first
      sequence) and an absolutely positioned fo:block-container (second sequence), each followed by unmarked
      blocks starting part-way down page 2. Page 3 takes the marked part's master in both.
    </p>
  </info>
  <fo>
